       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is twice the usual maximum for adults:\n- Immediate-release maximum: 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- Extended-release maximum: 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n\nAt this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum). 1700 mg may be a typo for this.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n- **1700 mg three times daily as written.** If this is deliberate, confirm it and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you reviewed the dose.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
      }
     ],
